# Expectation record for 09_optimization_levels/002_loop_invariance.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 002_loop_invariance
area               = 09_optimization_levels
description        = Loop results unchanged under invariant motion, strength reduction and unrolling at -O0, -O1 and -O2
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Free of undefined and unspecified behaviour. No signed overflow anywhere: every loop bound
is at most 1000 and every accumulator stays far inside int range, the largest being
sum_big at 499500, which is about 0.02 percent of INT_MAX. Every induction variable is
bounded by 1000 and is assigned before every use, so there is no read of uninitialized
storage. The only division is i % 3, whose divisor is non-zero and whose dividend is
non-negative. No shift operator appears. No pointer arithmetic, no aliasing violation, no
object modified twice between sequence points, at most one side-effecting argument per
call, and no dependence on padding bytes or on relative addresses.
Several volatile objects are read within a single expression; their relative order is
unspecified, but no volatile object is modified anywhere in the program, so every read of
a given object yields the same value and the printed output does not depend on the
ordering.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
No implementation-defined behaviour is observed. Widths are normalized: only int is used,
which is 32 bits on all four targets, and long is never used because sizeof(long) is 4 on
i686 and 8 on the other three targets. Plain char is not used, so the measured plain-char
signedness difference (signed on x86-64 and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64)
cannot be observed. No address, pointer value, sizeof or _Alignof result is printed. No
floating point is used. Loop bounds and factors are read from volatile storage, so no loop
can be folded into a constant and the backend must emit real loop code at every
optimization level.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
sum_mul=135
sum_inv=210
sum_pow2=360
sum_big=499500
down=55
once=5
nested=1540
guarded=147
END
